  "body": "Stacked on #1219 (on #1137, #1045, #1005). Retarget to `main` before #1219 merges.\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Kernel** (`camcraft-motion`, `machining2d::thread_mill`): `ThreadParams` gains `r_z: Option<f64>`, the R plane. Each feature's rapid stops at `max(R, the ride's run-out)` and the feed down the axis (or beside the boss) starts there; the ride climbs back to it at feed before the link rapid. `None` is the #894 ride, so every existing kernel golden is byte-identical. An R plane below a feature's top, above the link plane, or not finite is refused by name.\n- **App** (`thread_op::kernel_params`): passes the resolved `top_z` (\"R plane (feed starts here)\") as `r_z`, for internal and external threads.\n- **Door** (new `operation::thread_r_plane`): a fixed `top_z` below a listed hole's or boss's top is refused when the operation is created, edited or re-tooled. A referenced height resolves at generate, where the kernel asks. The door's R check runs after the tool and feature laws, so their refusals keep their own wording.\n- **Stock law** (`thread_r_plane::judge`, called at generate before the #992/#985 way-in laws): every vertical rapid down is read in the prior grid over the mill's full disc. Stock above the rapid's end is refused by name with the stock height and the fix (\"raise the R plane (feed starts here) to z ... or above, or machine that stock away\"). An unknown prior or an unreadable disc is left to the way-in laws, which already refuse both by name.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1212-thread-r-plane.md`. It covers how the default is seeded: unchanged, Top of Model, and every golden fixture already states R on the feature top.\n\n## Tests (pinning)\n\n- Kernel: `machining2d::thread_tests::the_ride_rapids_to_the_r_plane_and_starts_its_feed_there` (internal and external; an R on the top equals the #894 ride move for move), `an_r_plane_under_a_top_or_over_the_link_plane_is_refused_by_name`.\n- Golden (new): `golden_cl::thread_mill_raised_r_plane_matches_golden` -> `tests/golden/thread_mill_raised_r_plane.cl` (R 2 mm over the tops of two holes). **No existing golden moved.**\n- App: `thread_entry::the_operations_r_plane_is_where_the_rapid_stops_and_the_feed_starts` (generates, verifies clean, posts through the gate), `an_r_plane_under_the_holes_top_is_refused_when_the_operation_is_made`, `an_r_plane_that_ends_the_rapid_in_the_stock_left_ahead_is_refused_by_name`. Unit: `operation::thread_r_plane::tests::*` (door, stock law).\n- Fixture changes: two MCP tests (`mcp::thread_milling_over_the_tools`, `external_thread_milling_over_the_tools`) typed a mouth at z 20 above a 15 mm block, under the default R (top of model). They now sit on the block's top, and the #992/#985 refusals they pin are unchanged. `thread_boss::impossible_bosses_are_refused_when_the_operation_is_made` states R on its 25 mm boss so that the reach refusal it pins is still the one reported.\n\nQuick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/988-thread-pass-control` on the final head: green (2 steps, 0 failed, 4.1 min) on cfb25dd2. Clippy `-D warnings` on camcraft-motion and camcraft-app: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Through the UI page: the Heights tab already shows the R plane, and no UI code changed.\n- Posted NC golden with a raised R plane: the CL golden pins the moves, and the post is unchanged.\n\nChangelog: Thread milling rapids to and starts its feed at the operation's R plane (top_z) instead of each hole's or boss's top; an R plane below a feature's top, or one whose rapid would end in stock left by the program ahead, is refused by name.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1212\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
